# Extracting separated radii from interval-covering data

The annulus sharpness construction needs actual separated members of a radius
set, rather than merely the lower bound on a covering number supplied by the
Minkowski definition.  The metric covering-number API gives a finite maximal
separated set; the lemma below converts its closed-ball cover back to the
closed interval convention used by `intervalCoveringNumber`.
